---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { experience } from '../data/portfolio';
---
<Base title="About" description="How Aryan Basantani connects computer science, finance, product work and the interests outside it.">
  <header class="page-head about-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>A little more about me.</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="about-prose">
    <p>I studied Computer Science at BITS Pilani, Hyderabad, alongside a minor in Finance. I chose that combination because I wanted to understand both how systems work and what their decisions change: the cost, the risk, and the experience of the people using them. My college work moved between software, equity research, portfolio modelling and student consulting, but I kept returning to the same kind of problem—taking something messy and making it useful to someone else.</p>

    <p>My roles gave that instinct different settings. At JPMorgan, I saw how much trust matters in financial workflows. At MoveInSync, I worked closer to customers, engineers and live operational data; a metric was only useful if the team could understand it and act on the records behind it. Kearney widened the view to enterprise technology decisions and the trade-offs involved in modernisation. Together, those experiences made me more interested in product work that stays close to both the system and the user.</p>

    <p>I’m looking for product management and technical PM roles in technology companies and startups. Fintech is a natural overlap for me, while markets and risk remain analytical directions I continue to explore. I enjoy understanding a problem, working through its constraints with engineers and then staying close enough to see whether what we shipped actually helped.</p>

    <p>Outside work, I follow Formula 1 for the contest on track and the engineering decisions underneath it. I tend to like anime and films with strong internal worlds—Dragon Ball Z, Monster, Psycho-Pass, Frieren, Cowboy Bebop and Neon Genesis Evangelion are favourites. I also keep an eye on oil, geopolitics and semiconductor supply, partly because large systems eventually show up in ordinary prices. Joe Hisaishi, Hans Zimmer, Iktara, anime themes, KK and Atif Aslam are usually somewhere in the background.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="about-credentials" aria-labelledby="credentials-title">
    <p class="mono">EDUCATION & CREDENTIALS</p><h2 id="credentials-title">BITS Pilani, Hyderabad Campus</h2>
    <p>B.E. Computer Science · Minor in Finance · 2020–2024</p><p>Overall CGPA 8.52/10 · Finance minor GPA 9.67/10</p>
    <ul><li>CFA Program: Level II cleared</li><li>FRM exams: Parts I and II cleared</li><li>Bloomberg Market Concepts</li></ul>
  </section>

  <section id="experience" class="about-experience" aria-labelledby="experience-title">
    <header class="about-experience-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Professional experience</p>
      <h2 id="experience-title">The roles behind the story.</h2>
      <p>Four settings that brought me closer to financial systems, customers, engineers and enterprise decisions.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="experience-page" aria-label="Professional timeline">
      {experience.map((job, index) => <article>
        <div class="experience-marker"><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
        <div class="experience-heading"><p class="mono">{job.dates}</p><h3>{job.company}</h3><p>{job.role}</p></div>
        <div class="experience-detail"><p>{job.detail}</p>{job.href && <a href={job.href}>Explore selected work <Icon /></a>}</div>
      </article>)}
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="page-next" aria-label="Continue exploring"><a href="/work/">Work and projects <Icon /></a><a href="/interests/">Interests <Icon /></a></nav>
</Base>
